# The same bytes on every system: Windows checkouts too keep LF, so test
# fixtures (tests/programs/*.expected), program hashes and the journal's
# examples match. (Calyx itself also reads `\r\n` sources as `\n`.)
* text=auto eol=lf

*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.zip binary
# Fuzz inputs are bytes, not text.
runtime/fuzz/corpus/** -text
